  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AZE: GARADAGH CEMENT EXPANSION AND ENERGY EFFICIENCY PROJECT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will expand the production capacity of an integrated cement facility from 2,616 tons of clinker per day to 4,000 tons per day and replace the existing four wet-type kilns with one modern dry-type kiln, raising the annual production of cement from 1.3 million tons per annum (TPA) to 1.7 million TPA. The more efficient dry kiln will reduce specific fuel consumption per unit of clinker produced. The project also includes reopening a limestone quarry and upgrading the cement mills, storage facilities, and associated production infrastructure.</narrative>
  </description>
